      "location": "proctor/src/main/java/com/pte/proctor/repository/ProctorSessionRepository.java",
      "evidence": "findByPublicIdAndProctorPublicId() and findBySessionPublicIdAndProctorPublicIdAndStatus() lacked tenantId filtering, so a user who is a proctor in one tenant and something else in another could reach a ProctorSession/ViolationEvent chain across tenants by publicId.",
      "why_it_matters": "Would let a cross-tenant caller issue force-submit/extend-time commands or read violation history against attempts outside their own tenant.",
      "required_action": "Replaced both repository methods with tenant-scoped equivalents (findByPublicIdAndProctorPublicIdAndTenantId, findBySessionPublicIdAndProctorPublicIdAndTenantIdAndStatus); threaded caller.tenantId() through ProctorSessionService.open/close/findOwned and both call sites (ProctorCommandService, ViolationService).",
      "owner": "cook"
    },
    {
      "id": "QUAL-002",
      "severity": "MEDIUM",
      "rule": "AUTH_ENFORCEMENT",
      "status": "RESOLVED",
      "introduced_by_current_change": true,
      "applicable": true,
      "confidence": "high",
      "location": "proctor/src/main/java/com/pte/proctor/controller/ProctorStompController.java",
      "evidence": "The three @MessageMapping handlers had no PROCTOR role check; @PreAuthorize does not enforce reliably on @MessageMapping methods under this STOMP configuration.",
      "why_it_matters": "A non-PROCTOR authenticated user could invoke the STOMP handlers; only an implicit ownership check stopped them, producing wrong error semantics (404 instead of 403) and an inconsistency with the REST endpoints' explicit role checks.",
      "required_action": "Added an explicit hasRole(\"PROCTOR\") check inside the single currentUser(Principal) helper every handler routes through, throwing a new ProctorRoleRequiredException (403) on failure — one enforcement point, not three.",
      "owner": "cook"
    },
    {
      "id": "QUAL-003",
      "severity": "MEDIUM",
      "rule": "CORS_POLICY",
      "status": "RESOLVED",
